---
/** Explain current flower responsibilities while preserving the earlier roster's provenance. */
import ResourceAbout from "../../components/ResourceAbout.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import AgenticNav from "../../components/AgenticNav.astro";
import LearningEngineeringFlower from "../../components/LearningEngineeringFlower.astro";
import catalog from "../../data/lifecycle/flower-catalog.json";
import historical from "../../data/lifecycle/resolved-roles.json";
const flower = catalog.flower;
const conditions = [
  ["Full team", "Retain the configured assignments and available members.", "Reference contribution schedule."],
  ["Domain omitted everywhere", "Withdraw the selected domain’s explicit instructions from every member.", "Retain members and contribution slots."],
  ["Domain withdrawn from one member", "Withdraw that domain from one selected member; other assignments remain.", "Retain this member’s contribution slots; overlap may compensate."],
  ["Member removed", "Remove the selected member’s contributions and all of their assigned domains.", "Report reduced work capacity separately."],
  ["One agent with matched slots", "One identity covers the reference team’s contribution and coordination slots.", "Match opportunities and the duties exposed at each slot."],
];
---
<Base title="Learning engineering flower · Capability Matters" description="Eight starting expertise domains, shared understanding, responsibilities to learners and stakeholders, and controlled team comparisons.">
  <AgenticNav active="roles" />
  <header class="container-wide intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Agentic learning engineering · Team framework</p>
    <h1>The learning engineering flower</h1>
    <ResourceAbout resource="agentic-roles" />
    <p>Learning engineering brings complementary expertise together around a shared challenge. The flower places <strong>shared understanding</strong> at the center and connects the whole team with <strong>learners and other stakeholders</strong>.</p>
    <nav class="page-links" aria-label="Flower guide"><a href="#domains">Eight starting domains</a><a href="#shared">Shared responsibilities</a><a href="#comparisons">Five comparisons</a><a href="#historical">Historical role contracts</a></nav>
  </header>
  <div class="container-wide roles">
    <LearningEngineeringFlower />
    <section id="domains" aria-labelledby="domains-heading">
      <h2 id="domains-heading">Expertise contributes to the work</h2>
      <p>The default simulation assigns one member to each domain and a coordinator. A particular challenge may need a different mix. One person can contribute several domains, and several people can share a domain. These editable instructions organize contributions; they do not establish anyone’s professional competence.</p>
      <div class="domain-grid">{flower.domains.map((domain, index) => <article id={domain.id}>
        <p class="eyebrow">Domain {index + 1}</p><h3>{domain.name}</h3><p>{domain.description}</p>
      </article>)}</div>
      <p class="source">Source: <a href={flower.source.url}>Ali and colleagues, Learning engineering is a team sport (2025)</a>. The flower domains are starting points and are not conclusive. Composition may shift with the challenge and stage.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="shared" aria-labelledby="shared-heading">
      <h2 id="shared-heading">The center is everyone’s responsibility</h2>
      <ul>{flower.shared_responsibilities.map(duty => <li>{duty}</li>)}</ul>
      <p>Assigning a responsibility does not substitute for involving learners, practitioners, and other stakeholders. Every configuration should distinguish supplied facts, proposed interpretations, and information still needed from those people.</p>
      <div class="distinctions">
        <article><h3>Flower domains</h3><p>Organize the expertise contributing to a team’s design work.</p></article>
        <article><h3>LENS foundations</h3><p><strong>Human flourishing, Learning sciences, and Systems engineering</strong> remain the three foundations of the program’s approach.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Evidence scorecard</h3><p><strong>Human flourishing support, system performance, and learning</strong> are assessed separately. They describe the design and available evidence; human outcomes need evaluation with people.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="comparisons" aria-labelledby="comparisons-heading">
      <h2 id="comparisons-heading">Five comparisons ask different questions</h2>
      <p>Distinguish a missing responsibility from losing a member’s time and contribution opportunities. Fix the case facts, challenge schedule, execution settings, and coordination policy, then inspect what each contrast actually changes.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Five flower comparison conditions"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Condition</th><th scope="col">Change</th><th scope="col">Capacity and interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>{conditions.map(row => <tr>{row.map((cell, index) => index === 0 ? <th scope="row">{cell}</th> : <td>{cell}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <p>The default full team schedules forty calls across Understand, Map, Design, Build, Instrument, Experiment, Evaluate, and Refine: four contributions from each domain and eight coordinator decisions. Removing one default domain member leaves thirty-six calls; the other default conditions retain forty. Custom schedules must be resolved before comparison.</p>
      <p>Overlap may allow another member to identify a concern. Omission does not erase a model’s latent knowledge, and no condition is programmed to fail. Matching calls also does not match token volume, independent perspectives, or human effort.</p>
      <p><a class="primary-link" href="/agentic-le/experiments/">Configure and compare flower teams</a></p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="evidence-heading">
      <h2 id="evidence-heading">Inspect the design and its evidence</h2>
      <p>The current protocol carries the shared case and integrated stage records into review. Keep the executable Build separate from later proposals: a recommendation to repair an artifact is not evidence that the repair was implemented. Freeze evidence-based ratings before revealing assignments.</p>
      <p>The completed flower study reports actual generated solutions, fixed browser observations, and frozen model reviews for the five comparisons. Read the three axes separately, retain unknown values, and inspect each candidate’s source and evidence. These records do not establish human learning or causal effects in human teams.</p>
      <p><a href="/agentic-le/flower-study/">Inspect the completed study and prototypes</a> · <a href="/agentic-le/paper/">Read Exploring the learning engineering flower with agentic simulation</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/tree/main/docs/lifecycle">Read the execution and evaluation documentation</a></p>
    </section>
    <details id="historical" class="historical">
      <summary>Historical roster and role contracts</summary>
      <p>These profiles document the earlier replay collection. Their original duties and requested LENS targets remain attached to those saved runs. They are not a crosswalk from the flower domains to a validated competency framework.</p>
      <nav class="page-links" aria-label="Historical role directory">{Object.entries(historical.roles).map(([id, role]) => <a href={`#${id}`}>{role.name}</a>)}</nav>
      {Object.entries(historical.roles).map(([id, role]) => <article id={id}><p class="eyebrow">Earlier roster</p><h3>{role.name}</h3><p>{role.competency}</p><details><summary>Original responsibilities</summary><ul>{role.duties.map(duty => <li>{duty}</li>)}</ul></details></article>)}
      <p>Registry {historical.registry_version}; framework {historical.framework_version}. Requested targets have no demonstrated proficiency evidence by themselves.</p>
      <p><a href="/agentic-le/record/?file=%2Fagentic-le%2Froles.json">Inspect the original resolved role contract</a> · <a href="/agentic-le/replay/">Open a historical replay</a></p>
    </details>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .intro{padding-top:1.4rem;padding-bottom:1rem}.intro h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);margin-bottom:.7rem}.intro>p:last-of-type{max-width:58rem}.page-links{display:flex;gap:.7rem 1.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.95rem}.roles{padding-bottom:3rem}.roles section{margin:2.5rem 0}.roles section,.roles article,#historical{scroll-margin-top:7rem}.domain-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1.4rem 0}.distinctions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin-top:1.4rem}article{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1.2rem;border-radius:8px;background:var(--bg)}article .eyebrow{margin:0 0 .5rem}article h3{font-size:1.2rem;margin:0 0 .8rem}article p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}.source{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted)}.table-scroll{overflow-x:auto;margin:1.5rem 0}table{width:100%;min-width:42rem;font-size:.93rem}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:.85rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}th{font-family:var(--sans)}tbody th{min-width:11rem}thead{background:var(--tint)}.primary-link{display:inline-block;padding:.7rem 1rem;background:var(--ink);color:white;border-radius:5px;font-family:var(--sans);text-decoration:none}.historical{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1.25rem}.historical>summary{font:700 1.15rem var(--sans);cursor:pointer}.historical article{margin:1rem 0}.historical>p:first-of-type{margin-top:1rem}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible,.table-scroll:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent-2);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:760px){.domain-grid,.distinctions{grid-template-columns:1fr}th,td{padding:.65rem}.table-scroll{font-size:.85rem}}
</style>
